{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_420132660", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article claims that Sam Panopoulos invented the Hawaiian pizza in 1962, but historical records show that pizza had been a staple in Italian communities across North America since at least the early 20th century.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_565495028#8_805625447"]}, {"text": "The article states that Panopoulos was the first to combine ham and pineapple on a pizza, but food historians dispute this claim, with Frank Pezzolo in Detroit being widely credited with its creation.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_579132576#11_1393128118"]}, {"text": "The article lacks primary sources or documents to verify Panopoulos' account, making it difficult to confirm his claim of inventing the Hawaiian pizza in 1962.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1128213278#2_1274782154"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1440134319", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Jenny Hills is described as a nutritionist and medical writer in the article, but no specific credentials or professional certifications are provided.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1441480674#6_2560206155"]}, {"text": "The article does not disclose any known conflicts of interest or affiliations that could affect Jenny Hills' work.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1441480674#6_2560206155"]}, {"text": "Dr. Braden Kuo's study compared instant ramen noodles to homemade ramen noodles by having a participant consume each type and then observing their digestive processes through a camera placed in the stomach.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1441480674#6_2560206155"]}, {"text": "The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has approved TBHQ for use in food at levels up to 0.02% of the total oil content, based on extensive research indicating it poses no significant health risks when consumed within these limits.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_724114240#3_1517613463"]}, {"text": "The article does not mention any additional research plans by Dr. Braden Kuo after his initial study comparing instant and homemade ramen noodles.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1441480674#6_2560206155"]}, {"text": "The article does not provide information about known health risks or benefits associated with Tertiary-butyl hydroquinone (TBHQ) found in packaged ramen noodles beyond the FDA's approval for use at specific levels.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_724114240#3_1517613463"]}, {"text": "The article does not mention any other studies comparing the digestion of processed foods like instant ramen to their fresh counterparts.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1441480674#6_2560206155"]}]}
