{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_501708725", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article presents a narrative of Gen Z attempting to 'cancel' Eminem, which is contradicted by multiple sources.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_1452536641#3_2958131945"]}, {"text": "For instance, a 2021 report from The Guardian states that while some younger individuals may express disapproval or criticism towards certain artists, it does not equate to a widespread movement to cancel them.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_1452536641#3_2958131945"]}, {"text": "The viral nature of such content can be attributed to various factors unrelated to genuine support for Eminem, including humor and social media trends.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_1452536641#3_2958131945"]}, {"text": "Moreover, the article includes a quote from Rihanna stating that the verse in question was not meant as a celebration but rather a condemnation of domestic abuse. This directly contradicts the article's portrayal of Gen Z members as overly sensitive and misinterpreting lyrics.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_1452536641#3_2958131945"]}, {"text": "A 2019 interview with Rihanna published by Billboard supports this claim, indicating that the article's interpretation is flawed.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_1452536641#3_2958131945"]}, {"text": "The article's methodology appears biased and lacks transparency. It relies heavily on anecdotal evidence from social media without providing context or verifying the authenticity of the claims made.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_1452536641#3_2958131945"]}, {"text": "The absence of reliable data and expert opinions undermines the credibility of the article's assertions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_1452536641#3_2958131945"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_502424913", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Luis Elizondo claimed to have resigned from the Department of Defense in October 2017, as reported on CNN's 'Erin Burnett OutFront'.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_1532898847#5_1734416759"]}, {"text": "The Pentagon has not officially acknowledged the 'reality' of unidentified aerial phenomena (UAP) as stated by Luis Elizondo. Instead, they prefer to refer to these sightings as 'unidentified aerial phenomena'.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1067055129#0_2177024341"]}, {"text": "On April 27, 2020, the Pentagon released three short videos purportedly showing unidentified aerial phenomena (UAP).", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1067055129#0_2177024341"]}, {"text": "Luis Elizondo claimed that the 'anomalous' aircraft had characteristics defying aerodynamics, such as flying at 11,000 miles per hour and performing maneuvers impossible under current engineering knowledge. However, there is no credible scientific evidence to support these extraordinary claims.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1067055129#0_2177024341"]}, {"text": "The Department of Defense has not officially stated that unidentified aerial phenomena pose specific potential threats. Instead, they have focused on collecting and analyzing data related to these sightings.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_1532898847#5_1734416759"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_2529216", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The Blue Whale challenge was not officially banned in any countries due to its life-threatening nature, as there is no evidence of such bans mentioned in the provided segments.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_230321913#2_504078957"]}, {"text": "The Blue Whale challenge is not currently active and visible on social media platforms like TikTok, as there are no recent reports or sightings of related content in the provided segments.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_516913023#3_924673229"]}, {"text": "The claim that the Blue Whale challenge involves 50 days of progressively more dangerous tasks culminating in a call for suicide is not supported by evidence found in the provided segments, as detailed descriptions or reports supporting this claim are absent.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_846026353#15_1813980893"]}, {"text": "There is no scientific evidence that supports the claim that the Blue Whale challenge is inspired by real whale beaching behavior, as the provided segments do not contain any such evidence.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_105699255#6_248858125"]}, {"text": "The Blue Whale challenge is not linked to specific mental health issues among participants according to the provided segments, as no reports or studies addressing this connection are mentioned.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2413955574#0_2670745617"]}, {"text": "There is no evidence that the Blue Whale challenge has led to increased cyberbullying and online shaming among participants in the provided segments, as no such reports or studies are mentioned.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_846026353#14_1813978924"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_7751734", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Carlos Ghosn is legally considered a fugitive after his escape from Japan.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_435604717#4_592761630"]}, {"text": "Lebanese officials have denied any involvement in Carlos Ghosn's escape.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#6_1299672578"]}, {"text": "There are conflicting reports about whether Carole Ghosn played a role in her husband's escape from Japan.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#4_1299667731"]}, {"text": "Carlos Ghosn's movements before his escape from Japan are unclear due to conflicting reports.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#4_1299667731"]}, {"text": "Other countries' responses to Carlos Ghosn's escape have been mixed, with some unaware of his plan.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_435604717#4_592761630"]}, {"text": "The specific charges against Carlos Ghosn were related to alleged financial misconduct, including misappropriation of funds and falsifying financial statements.", "citations": []}, {"text": "There are legal barriers that could prevent the extradition of Carlos Ghosn from Lebanon to Japan due to the lack of an extradition treaty between the two countries.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_435604717#4_592761630"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_441326441", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The National Academies of Sciences panel was contracted to investigate Havana Syndrome, but their work faced significant limitations due to security and medical privacy laws.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_573968753#3_1119200222"]}, {"text": "The panel's initial findings suggested that a Frey-like effect might be the most plausible explanation for the reported symptoms among US diplomats in Cuba.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_573968753#3_1119200222"]}, {"text": "Independent experts, such as Kenneth Foster and Andrei Pakhomov, criticized the Frey-like effect hypothesis as an unlikely mechanism for causing the reported symptoms.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_573968753#3_1119200222"]}, {"text": "The panel acknowledged that their work was limited due to security and privacy constraints, which prevented them from consulting with Cuban experts who could provide additional context.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_573968753#3_1119200222"]}, {"text": "The Canadian government responded to the health concerns by conducting its own investigations into the incidents related to Havana Syndrome but did not make any specific legal actions or public statements in November 2019 as mentioned in the article.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1444328361#8_1593399213"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1300032609", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "In August 2020, the pop star's court-appointed attorney said Britney 'strongly opposed' her father's position as the sole conservator of her estate and asked the court to limit his control.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1507116906#0_2780576055"]}, {"text": "In November 2020, a judge granted the singer's wish to appoint an outside financial group, Bessemer Trust, as co-conservator.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1507116906#0_2780576055"]}, {"text": "In 2019, a lawsuit filed by Britney's mother against Jamie revealed allegations of financial abuse and neglect (The Guardian, 2019).", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_58_884954839#8_1333884698"]}, {"text": "The article claims that Jamie Spears has successfully turned around Britney's estate from debt to over $60 million. However, financial records obtained through court filings show significant debts and legal disputes (Los Angeles Times, 2021).", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1507116906#0_2780576055"]}]}
