{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1165221603", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article claims that oxygen bars deliver 95% oxygen, but studies show they typically provide only about 30-40%.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_662415614#4_1371930334"]}, {"text": "Dr. Norman H. Edelman from the American Lung Association states that healthy individuals do not need extra oxygen because their blood is already saturated with it.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1310457346#0_2760754061"]}, {"text": "The article suggests that walking in nature provides a more natural and effective alternative, but it lacks scientific backing for this claim.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_662415614#3_1371928605"]}, {"text": "Dr. Jason Turowski notes that the numerous health claims made by oxygen bars do not hold merit, as they are based on anecdotal evidence and the placebo effect.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_220476565#6_508587947"]}, {"text": "The article fails to provide credible evidence for its assertions, relying instead on unverified claims and unsupported assertions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1725979408#5_3542892854"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1960853470", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article cites Dennis Hill and Kelly Hauf as examples of patients who allegedly cured their cancers with cannabis.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1960830169#14_3177674260"]}, {"text": "A comprehensive review by the National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine found insufficient evidence to support the use of cannabis for cancer treatment.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_652628650#4_1623928866"]}, {"text": "Dr. Abrams from UCSF Osher Center for Integrative Medicine is quoted as being cautious about assuming cannabis cures cancer, noting that he would expect more survivors if it definitively cured the disease.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_358924403#14_443662024"]}, {"text": "The article mentions laboratory and animal studies showing that cannabinoids like CBD and THC can kill cancer cells without harming healthy cells, but these findings are not enough to conclude that cannabis can cure human cancers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_122645132#18_224182660"]}, {"text": "GreenState is known for promoting pro-cannabis content and may be biased in its reporting, lacking transparency regarding funding sources.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1960830169#14_3177674260"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_654618974", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Healthline's article on the Mandela effect does not consider all possible cognitive biases and psychological factors that could explain these phenomena, such as confirmation bias or social influence.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1233762358#0_2788409754"]}, {"text": "The article does not mention cognitive dissonance as an explanation for why people might hold onto false memories despite contradictory evidence.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1233762358#0_2788409754"]}, {"text": "Healthline does not discuss confirmation bias as a factor in people's tendency to only seek out information that confirms their preconceived notions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1233762358#0_2788409754"]}, {"text": "The article does not mention brain damage or disorders like Alzheimer's as potential causes of confabulation in people experiencing the Mandela effect.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1233762358#0_2788409754"]}, {"text": "Healthline does not discuss misattribution of memory as a factor in people confusing the source of their memories.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1233762358#0_2788409754"]}, {"text": "The article does not mention fake news as a potential explanation for why people might believe false information.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1233762358#0_2788409754"]}, {"text": "Healthline does not discuss the role of cognitive dissonance in people's resistance to accepting evidence that contradicts their beliefs.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1233762358#0_2788409754"]}, {"text": "The article does not mention time travel or parallel universes as possible theories to explain the Mandela effect, focusing instead on confabulation and false memories.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1233762358#0_2788409754"]}, {"text": "Healthline does not discuss the concept of d\u00e9j\u00e1 vu as an explanation for why people might feel like they've experienced something before when they haven't, which could be relevant to understanding false memories.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1233762358#0_2788409754"]}, {"text": "The article does not mention quantum mechanics as a basis for Fiona Broome's theory of parallel universes and the Mandela effect, instead attributing the phenomenon to confabulation and false memories.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1233762358#0_2788409754"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_1430382251", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The 2019 Nature study did not revive any brain functions to a level where awareness or consciousness was restored.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181590967#3_376417822"]}, {"text": "The 2019 BrainEx study did not report any signs of consciousness or awareness in the treated brains.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181590967#3_376417822"]}, {"text": "The 2019 BrainEx study focused on maintaining cellular function without achieving full recovery and did not report any signs of consciousness or awareness.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181590967#3_376417822"]}, {"text": "The 2019 BrainEx study did not demonstrate any recovery from irreversible damage and the implications for organ donation and clinical practice remain speculative.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181590967#3_376417822"]}, {"text": "The 2019 BrainEx study did not report any specific findings regarding brain cell death and activity beyond maintaining cellular function without achieving full recovery.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181590967#3_376417822"]}, {"text": "The 2019 BrainEx study did not use drugs to prevent neuronal firing in the revived pig brains; instead, it aimed to prevent any signs of awareness and focused on maintaining cellular function without achieving full recovery.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181590967#3_376417822"]}, {"text": "The 2019 BrainEx study did not raise any ethical concerns among researchers; rather, it focused on preventing any signs of awareness and maintaining cellular function without achieving full recovery.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181590967#3_376417822"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_273997000", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Citibank's spokeswoman declined to comment on the $900 million payment mistake.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_900269694#2_1940844801"]}, {"text": "Revlon stated that it did not pay down the loan or any portion of it, suggesting a clerical error by Citibank.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_900269694#2_1940844801"]}, {"text": "Citibank has launched an internal investigation into the matter, indicating they are addressing the issue.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_900269694#2_1940844801"]}, {"text": "Several hedge funds, including Brigade Capital Management, Symphony Asset Management and HPS Investment Partners, are refusing to return the $900 million payment mistake.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_900269694#2_1940844801"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_515083157", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "NASA scientists claim to have discovered evidence of a parallel universe where time moves backwards, but this is highly speculative and lacks substantial scientific backing.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_515098435#0_920079682"]}, {"text": "The ANITA experiment has detected unusual signals, but these findings do not definitively support the parallel universe theory.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_515098435#0_920079682"]}, {"text": "Geraint Lewis from the University of Sydney stated that there are multiple alternative explanations for the results from ANITA, suggesting that the data does not definitively support the parallel universe theory.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_96472339#0_113663797"]}, {"text": "Pat Scott, an astroparticle phenomenologist at the University of Queensland, expressed skepticism about the interpretation of the ANITA findings, noting that there's nothing necessarily making it a detection of a parallel universe.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1120669409#4_2365731473"]}, {"text": "The article lacks credible sources and peer-reviewed studies to support its claims, with only Peter Gorham from the University of Hawaii being cited as a key source.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_515098435#0_920079682"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_515287844", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The fire at Notre Dame Cathedral started around 6:50 PM local time on Monday night, or approximately 2:50 AM AEST.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_865179283#0_1710550023"]}, {"text": "Smoke was observed coming from the attic of Notre Dame Cathedral almost immediately after the alarm went off, indicating an early detection of the fire.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_865179283#0_1710550023"]}, {"text": "The French authorities are investigating the cause of the fire but have not yet determined whether it was accidental or due to other factors such as ongoing renovations.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_865179283#0_1710550023"]}, {"text": "There is no concrete evidence linking the Notre Dame Cathedral fire to recent attacks on Catholic churches in France, though such incidents have raised concerns about potential hostility towards religious symbols.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_865179283#0_1710550023"]}, {"text": "The French government has stated that they will determine the origin of the fire, though this process has not yet yielded any definitive conclusions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_865179283#0_1710550023"]}]}
