{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1289995263", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The New York Times reported a 17-year-old Florida hacker as the mastermind of the 2020 Twitter hack.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_753912797#2_1551768121"]}, {"text": "Wired magazine suggested Andrew \"Weev\" Auernheimer, involved in prior hacks, may have been responsible instead.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_698034230#12_1408535196"]}, {"text": "The New York Times has inaccuracies and biases, as studies from the University of Texas's News Integrity Initiative show.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#2_1840408564"]}, {"text": "Unverified statements from unnamed sources, like 'ever so anxious,' complicate verifying the article\u2019s claims.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_65683255#5_152682486"]}, {"text": "The Times lacked a detailed verification methodology for their 2020 Twitter hack reporting.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#5_1840414979"]}, {"text": "Sources were not specified, making credibility hard to assess.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_106764255#4_251896755"]}, {"text": "Details about the sequence of events in the 2020 Twitter hack were not provided.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_1079321515#1_1314864483"]}, {"text": "No mention of legal or ethical issues with The New York Times' coverage of the 2020 Twitter hack.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_32_981786416#5_1916853166"]}, {"text": "The Times has faced similar controversies in cybersecurity reporting, as past studies from the University of Texas show.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#1_1840406315"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_52_1666095905", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The initial plan for the European Super League was to have 20 teams, as mentioned in the article.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_607661422#6_656736776"]}, {"text": "The financial difficulties caused by the pandemic played a role in the decision to form the European Super League, as suggested by UK Prime Minister Boris Johnson's statement.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_607661422#6_656736776"]}, {"text": "Florentino Perez was a key leader involved in the proposed European Super League, serving as its president and making significant contributions to the initiative.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_607661422#6_656736776"]}, {"text": "The proposed European Super League included plans to provide enhanced solidarity payments to all football stakeholders, as stated by the official release of the initiative.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_607661422#6_656736776"]}, {"text": "The European Super League was initially listed as having 20 founding members, including key clubs such as Real Madrid and Manchester United.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_607661422#6_656736776"]}, {"text": "One of the goals of the proposed European Super League was to address and alleviate the financial challenges faced by football clubs due to the pandemic, as highlighted in various statements from club executives and government officials.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_607661422#6_656736776"]}, {"text": "Key leaders involved in the proposed European Super League included Florentino Perez as president and Joel Glazer as vice chairman of the initiative.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_607661422#6_656736776"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_304836636", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Historical examples of a shift to a cashless system, such as Sweden and India, have not uniformly led to increased efficiency and security.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_296154652#0_672316536", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1067298671#6_2378657137"]}, {"text": "Sweden's transition to a cashless system has not significantly reduced overall crime rates; non-cash crimes such as fraud and identity theft have increased.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_296154652#0_672316536"]}, {"text": "The Bank of England's study found that moving towards a cashless society could save up to \u00a3350 million annually in the UK alone, contradicting the article's claim that businesses and banks would incur significant costs.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_589076476#2_1390263515"]}, {"text": "In India, despite the demonetization effort, cash transactions quickly rebounded to pre-demonetization levels, indicating that the transition to a cashless society can be met with significant resistance and may not lead to the expected benefits.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1923848764#4_2074607111"]}, {"text": "The implementation of digital payment systems in countries with high informal economies has not uniformly led to increased tax collection; some regions saw a temporary increase followed by a return to cash transactions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_589076476#1_1390261359"]}, {"text": "Digital payment systems have not completely eliminated the problem of counterfeit money; while they reduce its prevalence, fake currency still exists in many economies.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1919486295#11_2070937475"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_1547893878", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article 'Birds: A Conspiracy Turned Movement' includes unrelated content about separation anxiety in pets, the invention of photography, and exposing kids to nature, which do not contribute to its main narrative.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_32_639106099#3_1185911772"]}, {"text": "There is no specific mention or discussion about separation anxiety in pets within the provided text.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_851697538#0_1744166558"]}, {"text": "The article mentions the United States Geological Survey (USGS) but does not provide specific details about its scientific studies or projects related to natural resources.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_747519998#8_1547129681"]}, {"text": "There is no mention of a conspiracy theory involving birds within the given articles.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_747519998#1_1547115786", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_239992739#0_478140214"]}, {"text": "The article does not provide detailed historical context on the invention and development of photography.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1736074117#0_3504574780"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_248024230", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article begins with a historical anecdote about Apple's founding, which is not directly relevant to the current legal dispute.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_34879208#8_89901277"]}, {"text": "Market dominance and monopoly claims are overly broad without specific evidence or data to support such sweeping statements.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_34879208#8_89901277"]}, {"text": "The article references the Sherman Act and California's Cartright Act without providing any context on how these laws apply to the case.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_34879208#8_89901277"]}, {"text": "The article mentions technical and contractual restrictions imposed by Apple but fails to provide concrete examples or evidence supporting these allegations.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_34879208#8_89901277"]}, {"text": "The article claims that users face high switching costs due to Apple's ecosystem but provides no data or analysis to support these assertions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_34879208#8_89901277"]}, {"text": "Throughout the document, there are numerous general statements without specific details or references to credible sources, which undermines the credibility of the claims made.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_34879208#8_89901277"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_933363597", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The claim that jackfruit is the largest tree fruit in the world is misleading, as there are other fruits like pumpkins and watermelons that surpass its size.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1007251276#3_1788166795"]}, {"text": "The article states that a single jackfruit can contain up to 500 seeds, but this claim is highly improbable and lacks scientific support.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1007251276#3_1788166795"]}, {"text": "A 2019 study published in the Journal of Food Science and Technology found that while jackfruit does contain significant amounts of vitamin C and B-complex vitamins, its nutritional profile is not superior to other fruits like oranges or pineapples.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1638235229#1_3137331358"]}, {"text": "The article's claim that jackfruit can help lower blood pressure due to high potassium content is questionable, as a 2018 systematic review in the Journal of Hypertension found limited and inconclusive evidence for specific fruits like jackfruit.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_808496648#0_1718127230"]}, {"text": "WebMD is a reputable health information provider, but the lack of transparent sourcing and the absence of peer-reviewed scientific evidence for many claims in this article cast doubt on its reliability.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_951007194#4_1940709463"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_8-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_58_748655897", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article 'The Area 51 Raid Was the Worst Way to Spot an Alien or UFO' by Sarah Scoles suggests a narrative that aligns with popular internet memes and viral trends rather than factual reporting.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_528666864#11_594051538"]}, {"text": "The author claims that revelers gathered near Area 51 hoping to spot UFOs or aliens, but this claim is not supported by official statements from law enforcement or local businesses in Nevada.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_528666864#11_594051538"]}, {"text": "The article states that security presence around Area 51 was 'friendly' and 'jovial,' with officers encouraging people to approach the gates, which directly conflicts with historical accounts and official statements from the U.S. Air Force.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_528666864#11_594051538"]}, {"text": "The author mentions seeing 'two triangular-looking somethings' flying over Area 51, but does not provide any corroborating evidence from official sources or independent witnesses to support this claim.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_528666864#11_594051538"]}, {"text": "The article's structure and content suggest a bias towards debunking conspiracy theories related to Area 51 without offering balanced perspectives, which may affect its overall credibility.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_528666864#11_594051538"]}]}
